{"ts": "2026-10-16T17:09:01.305543Z", "run_id": "r-20261016T1655Z-d3d9", "unit": "openspec:add-telemetry-runtime", "seq": 80, "type": "task.red_ok", "task": "1.2", "base": "8fc352eb04c846c27f41c99854f58e0a14e5802a", "tests": ["packages.core.tests.test_telemetry_metric_guard_wiring::test_metric_guard_wraps_the_console_exporter", "packages.core.tests.test_telemetry_metric_guard_wiring::test_metric_guard_wraps_the_otlp_exporter", "packages.core.tests.test_telemetry_metric_guard_wiring::test_unreachable_metric_collector_warns_once"], "frozen": [".gitignore", "conftest.py", "packages/core/tests/conformance/conftest.py", "packages/core/tests/fixtures/history/claude/-Users-test-projects-sample-project/aaaaaaaa-bbbb-cccc-dddd-eeeeeeeeeeee.jsonl", "packages/core/tests/fixtures/history/codex/rollout-2024-03-15T10-00-00-cccccccc-dddd-eeee-ffff-000000000001.jsonl", "packages/core/tests/fixtures/history/hermes/session_20240315_100000_aabbccdd.json", "packages/core/tests/fixtures/history/hermes/session_cron_test123_20240315_101000.json", "packages/core/tests/fixtures/history/kiro/workspace-sessions/L1VzZXJzL3Rlc3QvcHJvamVjdHMvc2FtcGxlLXByb2plY3Q/kkkkkkkk-llll-mmmm-nnnn-oooooooooooo.json", "packages/core/tests/fixtures/history/kiro/workspace-sessions/L1VzZXJzL3Rlc3QvcHJvamVjdHMvc2FtcGxlLXByb2plY3Q/sessions.json", "packages/core/tests/test_telemetry_metric_guard_wiring.py"], "notes": "RED for FB-002 / C-0f789a7e. New module packages/core/tests/test_telemetry_metric_guard_wiring.py has three tests, all tagged @pytest.mark.l4(\"C-0f789a7e\") and all failing by assertion on the current code (no TypeError/AttributeError). Two structural tests follow the metric exporter chain the reader received (provider._sdk_config.metric_readers -> reader._exporter, then _inner) and assert _GuardedMetricExporter wraps the OTLP/Console metric exporter; currently the chain has length 1 (raw exporter) so len==2 fails. The behavioural test points OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT at a closed port, records a counter and force_flushes three times, asserting exactly one WARNING 'telemetry: metric export failed' on mintmory.telemetry; currently zero are logged. I verified with a throwaway script (in agent-tmp, not the workspace) that once the guard wraps the OTLP metric exporter the same three force_flushes log exactly one such warning, so the test is discriminating and will pass in green. No production code, no stub, no noqa/type: ignore. Note: MeterProvider._all_metric_readers is a process-wide class-level WeakSet, so the helper reads the reader from the provider's own _sdk_config.metric_readers instead. The API-side unwrap of _inner in packages/api/tests/test_health_and_otel.py named in the finding is task 7.1, outside this task's criterion.", "criteria": {"C-0f789a7e": {"tests": ["packages.core.tests.test_telemetry_metric_guard_wiring::test_metric_guard_wraps_the_console_exporter", "packages.core.tests.test_telemetry_metric_guard_wiring::test_metric_guard_wraps_the_otlp_exporter", "packages.core.tests.test_telemetry_metric_guard_wiring::test_unreachable_metric_collector_warns_once"], "proof": "red_assertion", "discriminating": ["packages.core.tests.test_telemetry_metric_guard_wiring::test_metric_guard_wraps_the_console_exporter", "packages.core.tests.test_telemetry_metric_guard_wiring::test_metric_guard_wraps_the_otlp_exporter", "packages.core.tests.test_telemetry_metric_guard_wiring::test_unreachable_metric_collector_warns_once"]}}, "suppressions": [], "fix_unit": "add-telemetry-runtime-fix-1"}
